<title>LATVIA: WATCHDOG SEES PAN-BALTIC SECURITIES COOPERATION.</title>
<headline>WATCHDOG SEES PAN-BALTIC SECURITIES COOPERATION.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Latvia's markets watchdog the securities commission on Monday said that it expected a cooperation agreement in the autumn between the securities commissions of Latvia, Lithuania and Estonia.</p>
<p>The commission said in a statement that its chief Viktor Gustsons visited Tallinn last week to meet Estonian market officials.</p>
<p>It said that cooperation was discussed and that a protocal was prepared which may be signed in September.</p>
<p>&quot;It is also foreseen that Lithuania takes part in this process in the near future and an agreement on cooperation between the market instutitions of Latvia, Lithuania and Estonia may be accepted,&quot; the commission added.</p>
<p>-- Patrick Lannin, Riga newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
</text>
